# .vercelignore — WHAT `vercel deploy` UPLOADS, as an ALLOW-LIST (Oct 9, the first test deploy).
#
# Everything at the repo root is excluded, then only what the Vercel build needs is let back in. The repo
# root is a working directory — screenshots, screen recordings, review TSVs, research files, _exports, .env —
# and an allow-list means a new file dropped there is private by default rather than uploaded by default.
#
# The build (vercel.json) runs `node regenerate-data.js canonical.json` and then `npm run build`, so it needs
# the source JSON, the generator and its two imports, the app, and the one schema doc the generator reads
# (docs/hooker_json_schema_v*.md, for the tag vocabulary). static/data is REGENERATED on Vercel, so the local
# copy is never uploaded.
/*
!/src
!/static
!/canonical.json
!/regenerate-data.js
!/table-coords.mjs
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/.npmrc
!/vite.config.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/vercel.json
!/docs
/docs/*
!/docs/hooker_json_schema_v*.md

# generated on Vercel by regenerate-data.js — never upload the local build output
/static/data/*
!/static/data/tag-vocab.json

# working files that can land anywhere
**/Screenshot*
**/Screen Shot*
**/Screen Recording*
**/.DS_Store
